# Divide by Zero targets a spell "with mana value 1 or greater" (CR 115.1); a spell's mana value counts X as the value
# chosen for it (CR 202.3e). Bot2's Walking Ballista cast with X = 0 has mana value 0 on the stack and is refused; with
# X = 1 it is a creature spell of mana value 1, so it is returned to Bot2's hand (Bot1 declines both halves of Learn).
# The X = 0 Ballista enters with no counters and dies.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Divide by Zero
Island x15

[Bot1 Sideboard]
Firebending Lesson

[Bot2 Deck]
Island
Black Lotus
Walking Ballista
Walking Ballista
Island x12

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
Bot2.Hand.Walking Ballista.Cast(X: 0)
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
! Bot1.Hand.Divide by Zero.Cast(Stack.Walking Ballista)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot2.Hand.Walking Ballista.Cast(X: 1)
Bot1.Hand.Divide by Zero.Cast(Stack.Walking Ballista)
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Choose()
Bot1.Choose()
[T3 Bot1.Upkeep]

[Expect]
Stack.Count = 0
Bot2.Graveyard = Black Lotus; Walking Ballista
Bot2.Hand.Walking Ballista.Colors.Count = 0
Bot2.Battlefield = Island
Bot1.Graveyard = Divide by Zero; Black Lotus
